WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.097 --> 00:00:02.680
SPEAKER: Let's take a quick look
at how to use to Google Cloud

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:03.940
SQL proxy.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:07.820
Go to cloud.google.com, and
open up your Cloud console.

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:09.490
Go to the SQL section.

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:12.480
Here you can see your
Cloud SQL instances.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:15.520
If you don't have a Cloud SQL
instance, you can create one.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.530
Click your instance to be taken
to the Instance Overview page.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:20.930
Now, go to the
Access Control tab,

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:22.830
and then go to the Users tab.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.050
Specify a new root password.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.950
Go to the following
page to follow along

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:28.200
with the rest of the tutorial.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:31.260
Scroll down and
click Enable the API.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.840
Choose your project,
and click Continue.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.560
The API should now be enabled.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.250
Follow the installation
instructions

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:39.870
for your operating system.

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:43.530
Now run gcloud auth
application-default login.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:45.290
Go back to the
SQL overview page,

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:47.330
and copy the instance
connection name.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:50.000
Run the Cloud SQL proxy,
and pass in your instance

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:50.870
connection name.

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:56.030
At the end of the string, you
also want to type in =tcp:3306.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:58.180
You now have a direct
connection to Cloud SQL

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:00.340
through the local proxy.

